1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,008
The first week of March is the busiest week of Malika's year.

2
00:00:04,058 --> 00:00:09,192
Everyone buys flowers for the eighth, and she cannot answer every buyer alone.

3
00:00:09,242 --> 00:00:13,752
So she hires a helper for the week, and her accountant wants to see the payments too.

4
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:24,792
In Lesson 16, Malika became her shop's first admin, and in Lesson 19 its server got a login of its own, and this lesson gives the rest of her team their own logins and roles.

5
00:00:24,842 --> 00:00:26,976
The easy way is to share one login.

6
00:00:27,026 --> 00:00:31,680
I think it is the most common shortcut in small shops, and the most expensive one.

7
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:36,840
If the helper sends a refund to a friend, the record says only that the shop did it.

8
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:40,536
And when someone leaves, the password changes for everyone.

9
00:00:40,586 --> 00:00:42,888
So Malika opens Users.

10
00:00:42,938 --> 00:00:48,408
The page lists everyone who works in the portal, and says each person has exactly one role.

11
00:00:48,458 --> 00:00:50,280
There are four.

12
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:54,096
The admin can do everything, including the team and the settings.

13
00:00:54,146 --> 00:00:58,128
The accountant views and exports, and handles disputes.

14
00:00:58,178 --> 00:01:04,368
The operator views, exports, makes payment links, gives refunds and handles disputes.

15
00:01:04,418 --> 00:01:06,336
The observer only views.

16
00:01:06,386 --> 00:01:14,184
Malika clicks "Invite a user", types her helper's email and name, and sees the four roles, each with a short line on what it can do.

17
00:01:14,234 --> 00:01:16,512
She chooses Operator and sends it.

18
00:01:16,562 --> 00:01:19,080
The page says the invitation was sent.

19
00:01:19,130 --> 00:01:21,984
Nobody ever types another person's password.

20
00:01:22,034 --> 00:01:24,888
In the helper's inbox, the email has a link.

21
00:01:24,938 --> 00:01:30,072
The helper sets their own password, and scans a code with an authenticator app on their phone.

22
00:01:30,122 --> 00:01:33,984
That second step is there because an operator can give money back.

23
00:01:34,034 --> 00:01:35,856
Then they sign in.

24
00:01:35,906 --> 00:01:39,192
The menu shows Payments, and other pages for the work.

25
00:01:39,242 --> 00:01:41,280
But there is no Users item at all.

26
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:45,336
The operator cannot manage the team, so the screen does not offer it.

27
00:01:45,386 --> 00:01:49,632
Every action in the portal names the roles that may run it, and nothing more.

28
00:01:49,682 --> 00:01:53,568
That is least privilege: each person gets only what their job needs.

29
00:01:53,618 --> 00:01:58,368
So a stolen operator login cannot add new users or change settings.

30
00:01:58,418 --> 00:02:04,728
For her accountant, Malika picks the Accountant role: changing a role is one choice in a list.

31
00:02:04,778 --> 00:02:08,640
A role change takes effect at once, and the person is signed out.

32
00:02:08,690 --> 00:02:11,688
On the ninth of March, the rush is over.

33
00:02:11,738 --> 00:02:14,088
Malika clicks Block on her helper.

34
00:02:14,138 --> 00:02:20,808
A window asks first: they are signed out at once and can no longer sign in, and their past actions stay in the history.

35
00:02:20,858 --> 00:02:25,248
Every refund the helper gave still names the helper.

36
00:02:25,298 --> 00:02:29,832
Then, out of curiosity, Malika tries to block herself.

37
00:02:29,882 --> 00:02:31,704
She is the only admin.

38
00:02:31,754 --> 00:02:37,320
The window asks her to choose a new admin first, and the Block button stays grey until she does.

39
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:43,008
A merchant can never lose its last admin, so nobody is ever locked out of their own shop.

40
00:02:43,058 --> 00:02:48,240
A login each means every refund and every export names a real person.

41
00:02:48,290 --> 00:02:51,384
And a person who leaves loses access the same minute.

42
00:02:51,434 --> 00:02:53,952
Next: Malika's second website.
